  "label": "racist_hate_scene",
  "description": "A scene depicting a man in a Ku Klux Klan-style robe and hood, juxtaposed with text that expresses hatred toward Black people ('I hate when I see a black out in my neighborhood') while simultaneously offering a 'candle' — a symbol of appeasement or passive tolerance. The visual of the KKK imagery directly maps onto the hateful sentiment expressed in the text, creating an analogical link between the wearer's identity and the racist message. The scene is designed to convey and reinforce anti-Black racism by using the KKK as a symbol of white supremacist hate, while the 'offering a candle' is a sarcastic or ironic gesture that implies a false sense of moral superiority or reconciliation.",
